=begin
  Documentation: https://elanthipedia.play.net/Lich_script_repository#aesthene

  Solves the Aesthene's Close time-lock word puzzle: a five-letter word, six
  guesses, with Wordle-style feedback on every row.

  Usage:
    ;aesthene full   - walk to the apprentice Timekeeper, redeem one time slip,
                       ask for access, attune to the lock you are shown and
                       solve it. Run it again for the next slip.
    ;aesthene solve  - attune to (or resume) the time lock in your room and
                       solve it. Use this when you already have a redeemed pass.
    ;aesthene check  - read the lock in your room and list the answers that are
                       still possible. Whispers nothing.

  When a lock's answer is missing from the built-in list, the script says so
  and asks you to post it in the lich discord so it can be added for everyone.

  Settings:
    aesthene_lock_answers: words to add to the built-in answer list in
      data/base-aesthene.yaml, for answers the list does not have yet.
      Case-insensitive. Example:
        aesthene_lock_answers:
          - cloak
          - patch
=end

# Loads and normalizes the word lists the solver works from.
module AestheneWords
  # Every lock answer and guess is exactly five ASCII letters.
  VALID_WORD = /\A[A-Z]{5}\z/

  # Upcases and validates raw word-list entries.
  #
  # Entries are run through +to_s+ first, so YAML scalars that Psych loads as
  # other types (a bare +false+ for the word FALSE) still come back as words.
  #
  # @param entries [Array, String, nil] raw entries from YAML
  # @return [Array(Array<String>, Array<String>)] unique valid words, and the
  #   entries that were rejected, as written
  # @example
  #   AestheneWords.normalize(['cloak', ' Patch ', 'yo-yo'])
  #   # => [["CLOAK", "PATCH"], ["yo-yo"]]
  def self.normalize(entries)
    valid = []
    rejected = []
    Array(entries).each do |entry|
      word = entry.to_s.strip.upcase
      if word.match?(VALID_WORD)
        valid << word
      else
        rejected << entry.to_s
      end
    end
    [valid.uniq, rejected]
  end

  # Merges the built-in answers with a character's additions.
  #
  # @param builtin [Array<String>] answers from data/base-aesthene.yaml
  # @param additions [Array, String, nil] the aesthene_lock_answers setting
  # @return [Array(Array<String>, Array<String>)] the merged answer list, and
  #   the rejected additions
  def self.answers(builtin, additions)
    known, = normalize(builtin)
    extra, rejected = normalize(additions)
    [(known + extra).uniq, rejected]
  end

  # Normalizes the fallback dictionary, leaving out words already in the answer
  # list so they are never considered twice.
  #
  # @param dictionary [Array, nil] dictionary from data/base-aesthene.yaml
  # @param answers [Array<String>] normalized answer list
  # @return [Array<String>] fallback words
  def self.dictionary(dictionary, answers)
    words, = normalize(dictionary)
    words - answers
  end
end

# Parses the time-lock grid the game prints after every whisper and look.
#
# A grid looks like this, one row per guess, followed by status lines:
#
#    +-----+-----+-----+-----+-----+
#    |  1  |  2  |  3  |  4  |  5  |
#    +-----+-----+-----+-----+-----+
#    | _A_ | *E* | *I* | _O_ | *U* |
#    | ___ | ___ | ___ | ___ | ___ |
#    +-----+-----+-----+-----+-----+
#   [1 of the 6 rows are locked into place.]
#
# Other game lines (room traffic, spell messages, other scripts' echoes) can be
# interleaved with the grid, so a line only counts if it is a complete
# five-cell row.
module AestheneGrid
  # Rows on every lock; used until a status line says otherwise.
  DEFAULT_ROWS = 6

  # Tile marks: + right place, _ wrong place but in the word, * not in the word.
  MARKS = { '+' => :hit, '_' => :present, '*' => :absent }.freeze

  # A tile such as "_A_". The two marks must match, which parse_row checks:
  # a backreference here would always point at the first cell's group.
  CELL = /\s*([+_*][A-Za-z][+_*])\s*\|/
  ROW_PATTERN = /\A\s*\|#{CELL}#{CELL}#{CELL}#{CELL}#{CELL}\s*\z/
  HEADER_PATTERN = /\|\s*1\s*\|\s*2\s*\|\s*3\s*\|\s*4\s*\|\s*5\s*\|/
  LOCKED_PATTERN = /\[(\d+) of the (\d+) rows are locked into place\.\]/
  LEGEND_END_PATTERN = /\* indicates a wrong letter that isn't used in the final word/
  PROMPT_PATTERN = /LOOK at the lock for an update on your progress/
  SOLVED_PATTERN = /pulse with blue light and lock in place|for your assistance in locking away unstable temporal magics/
  WHISPERED_PATTERN = /You quietly whisper '(\w+)' to the lock/
  NOT_TASKED_PATTERN = /You are not currently tasked with solving the puzzle/
  NO_PASS_PATTERN = /To interact with the lock, you must redeem a pass for the event/

  # One guess and the mark on each of its five tiles.
  Row = Struct.new(:guess, :marks) do
    # @return [Array<Array(String, Symbol)>] [letter, mark] pairs in order
    def cells
      guess.chars.zip(marks)
    end

    # @return [Boolean] true when every tile is in the right place
    def solved?
      marks.all?(:hit)
    end
  end

  # Parses one game line as a grid row.
  #
  # @param line [String, nil] a game line
  # @return [Row, nil] the row, or nil when the line is not a filled row
  # @example
  #   AestheneGrid.parse_row(' | +P+ | _O_ | *A* | *C* | *H* |')
  #   # => #<struct Row guess="POACH", marks=[:hit, :present, :absent, :absent, :absent]>
  def self.parse_row(line)
    match = ROW_PATTERN.match(line.to_s)
    return nil unless match

    tiles = match.captures
    return nil unless tiles.all? { |tile| tile[0] == tile[2] }

    Row.new(tiles.map { |tile| tile[1].upcase }.join, tiles.map { |tile| MARKS.fetch(tile[0]) })
  end

  # Accumulates the game's response to one lock command.
  class Reading
    # @return [Array<Row>] rows of the most recent grid
    attr_reader :rows
    # @return [String, nil] the guess the game echoed back, upcased
    attr_reader :whispered

    # Starts an empty reading: no rows, and the default six rows free.
    def initialize
      @rows = []
      @locked = nil
      @total = DEFAULT_ROWS
      @whispered = nil
      @status = nil
      @legend_done = false
    end

    # Feeds one game line into the reading.
    #
    # @param line [String, nil] a game line
    # @return [void]
    def feed(line)
      line = line.to_s
      if (row = AestheneGrid.parse_row(line))
        @rows << row
      elsif line.match?(HEADER_PATTERN)
        # A new grid starts; drop rows from any earlier grid in the buffer.
        @rows = []
      elsif (match = LOCKED_PATTERN.match(line))
        @locked = match[1].to_i
        @total = match[2].to_i
      elsif (match = WHISPERED_PATTERN.match(line))
        @whispered = match[1].upcase
      elsif line.match?(LEGEND_END_PATTERN)
        @legend_done = true
      else
        @status ||= status_for(line)
      end
    end

    # @return [Symbol, nil] :solved, :prompt (ready for another guess),
    #   :not_tasked or :no_pass; nil while nothing decisive has been seen
    attr_reader :status

    # @return [Boolean] true once the full grid and its legend have arrived
    def grid_complete?
      !@locked.nil? && @legend_done
    end

    # @return [Boolean] true when the game reports every row used
    def out_of_rows?
      !@locked.nil? && @locked >= @total
    end

    # @return [Integer] rows still free for guesses
    def rows_left
      [@total - (@locked || @rows.size), 0].max
    end

    # @return [Boolean] true when the lock was solved
    def solved?
      @status == :solved || @rows.last&.solved? || false
    end

    # @return [Boolean] true when the row count in the status line matches the
    #   rows that were parsed (false means some rows were missed)
    def consistent?
      @locked.nil? || @locked == @rows.size
    end

    private

    # @param line [String] a game line
    # @return [Symbol, nil] the status the line signals, if any
    def status_for(line)
      case line
      when SOLVED_PATTERN then :solved
      when PROMPT_PATTERN then :prompt
      when NOT_TASKED_PATTERN then :not_tasked
      when NO_PASS_PATTERN then :no_pass
      end
    end
  end
end

# Narrows the possible answers from lock feedback and picks the next guess.
#
# Known answers come first: the solver only treats a dictionary word as a
# possible answer once feedback rules out every known answer. Guesses are
# hedged, though. While known answers remain, unlisted dictionary words still
# count at {HEDGE_WEIGHT} when scoring a guess, so the early rows also narrow
# the rare lock whose answer is not on the list yet. In simulation this left
# known answers unchanged (all solved, at most four guesses) and raised
# unlisted answers from 97.5% to 99.8% solved.
#
# Narrowing never depends on how the game marks a repeated letter. A guess with
# a repeated letter only rules out what both possible rules agree on: every
# tile's own position, plus an exact letter count when the same letter is both
# confirmed and starred in one row.
class AestheneSolver
  # Opening probes: twenty distinct common letters across four guesses. They
  # are only guessed when they split the candidates better than a real word.
  PROBES = %w[AEIOU TPMRS BCDGN FHKLW].freeze

  # Feedback code for five right-place tiles (2 in every base-3 digit).
  ALL_HIT = 242

  # How much an unlisted dictionary word counts, relative to a known answer,
  # when scoring a guess while known answers remain.
  HEDGE_WEIGHT = 0.02

  # Largest candidate set scored exhaustively; bigger sets are sampled so a
  # guess is still picked in a second or two.
  SCORING_LIMIT = 600

  # Dictionary words offered as guesses even though they cannot be the answer,
  # sampled evenly from the dictionary.
  PROBE_WORD_LIMIT = 2000

  # @return [Array<String>] answers still consistent with the feedback
  attr_reader :candidates

  # @param answers [Array<String>] normalized known lock answers
  # @param dictionary [Array<String>] normalized fallback words
  # @param opening [String, nil] first guess for an empty lock. Precomputed,
  #   because scoring the empty lock takes several seconds; nil computes it.
  def initialize(answers, dictionary, opening: nil)
    @answers = answers
    @dictionary = dictionary
    @opening = opening
    @rows = []
    @known = answers
    @unlisted = dictionary
    @candidates = answers.empty? ? dictionary : answers
  end

  # Re-derives the candidates from every row on the lock.
  #
  # Always works from the full grid rather than the newest row, so a missed or
  # repeated reading cannot leave stale state behind.
  #
  # @param rows [Array<AestheneGrid::Row>] every row on the lock
  # @return [Array<String>] the candidates
  def observe(rows)
    @rows = rows
    @known = @answers.select { |word| fits_all?(word) }
    @unlisted = @dictionary.select { |word| fits_all?(word) }
    @candidates = @known.empty? ? @unlisted : @known
  end

  # @return [Boolean] true when no known answer fits and the candidates come
  #   from the dictionary
  def fallback?
    @known.empty?
  end

  # Picks the guess most likely to solve the lock in the rows left.
  #
  # With one row left, it guesses a candidate. With two left, it maximizes the
  # chance that the final row is forced. Otherwise it minimizes the expected
  # weight of candidates left. Ties go to a guess that could itself be the
  # answer.
  #
  # @param rows_left [Integer] rows still free on the lock
  # @return [String, nil] the guess, or nil when nothing fits
  def next_guess(rows_left)
    return nil if @candidates.empty?
    return @candidates.first if @candidates.size == 1 || rows_left <= 1
    return @opening if @opening && @rows.empty?

    targets = weighted_targets
    pool = (unused_probes + sample(@candidates, SCORING_LIMIT) + @answers + probe_words).uniq
    candidate_set = @candidates.to_h { |word| [word, true] }
    pool.min_by.with_index do |guess, index|
      [score(guess, targets, rows_left), candidate_set[guess] ? 0 : 1, index]
    end
  end

  # Whether a word could still be the answer given one row of feedback.
  #
  # @param word [String] a candidate answer
  # @param row [AestheneGrid::Row] one guess and its marks
  # @return [Boolean]
  def self.fits?(word, row)
    row.cells.each_with_index do |(letter, mark), index|
      case mark
      when :hit then return false unless word[index] == letter
      when :present then return false if word[index] == letter || !word.include?(letter)
      when :absent then return false if word[index] == letter
      end
    end
    row.cells.group_by(&:first).all? do |letter, cells|
      marks = cells.map(&:last)
      next true unless marks.include?(:absent)

      word.count(letter) == marks.count { |mark| mark != :absent }
    end
  end

  # Wordle feedback for a guess against an answer, as a base-3 integer
  # (0 absent, 1 present, 2 hit per tile). Used only to score guesses.
  #
  # @param guess [String]
  # @param answer [String]
  # @return [Integer] 0..242; {ALL_HIT} when the guess is the answer
  def self.feedback_code(guess, answer)
    marks = Array.new(5, 0)
    spare = Hash.new(0)
    5.times do |i|
      if guess[i] == answer[i]
        marks[i] = 2
      else
        spare[answer[i]] += 1
      end
    end
    5.times do |i|
      next if marks[i] == 2 || spare[guess[i]].zero?

      marks[i] = 1
      spare[guess[i]] -= 1
    end
    marks.reduce(0) { |code, mark| (code * 3) + mark }
  end

  private

  # @param word [String]
  # @return [Boolean] true when the word fits every row seen so far
  def fits_all?(word)
    @rows.all? { |row| self.class.fits?(word, row) }
  end

  # @return [Array<String>] probes not yet guessed on this lock
  def unused_probes
    PROBES - @rows.map(&:guess)
  end

  # Known answers count fully; unlisted dictionary words count at
  # {HEDGE_WEIGHT} while known answers remain, and fully once none do.
  #
  # @return [Array<Array(String, Float)>] [word, weight] pairs to score against
  def weighted_targets
    unlisted_weight = @known.empty? ? 1.0 : HEDGE_WEIGHT
    @known.map { |word| [word, 1.0] } + sample(@unlisted, SCORING_LIMIT).map { |word| [word, unlisted_weight] }
  end

  # @return [Array<String>] evenly spaced dictionary words to try as guesses
  def probe_words
    @probe_words ||= sample(@dictionary, PROBE_WORD_LIMIT)
  end

  # @param words [Array<String>]
  # @param limit [Integer]
  # @return [Array<String>] up to limit words, evenly spaced
  def sample(words, limit)
    return words if words.size <= limit

    step = words.size.fdiv(limit)
    Array.new(limit) { |i| words[(i * step).floor] }
  end

  # Lower is better.
  #
  # @param guess [String]
  # @param targets [Array<Array(String, Float)>] weighted words to score against
  # @param rows_left [Integer]
  # @return [Float]
  def score(guess, targets, rows_left)
    # Per feedback: [total weight, heaviest single word].
    buckets = Hash.new { |hash, code| hash[code] = [0.0, 0.0] }
    targets.each do |word, weight|
      bucket = buckets[self.class.feedback_code(guess, word)]
      bucket[0] += weight
      bucket[1] = weight if weight > bucket[1]
    end
    # Two rows left: the final row guesses the likeliest word in its bucket,
    # so the chance of solving is the sum of each bucket's heaviest word.
    return -buckets.each_value.sum { |_total, heaviest| heaviest } if rows_left == 2

    buckets.sum { |code, (total, _heaviest)| code == ALL_HIT ? 0 : total * total }
  end
end

# Runs the Aesthene's Close time-lock event: redeems a slip, attunes to a lock
# and solves it.
#
# @note Optional setting: `aesthene_lock_answers` [Array<String>] answers to
#   add to the built-in list in data/base-aesthene.yaml.
#
# @example Redeem a slip and solve one lock
#   ;aesthene full
# @example Solve the lock in your room with a pass you already redeemed
#   ;aesthene solve
# @example See which answers are still possible
#   ;aesthene check
class Aesthene
  # Room with the apprentice Timekeeper, where slips are redeemed.
  TIMEKEEPER_ROOM = 16_958

  # Seconds to wait for the grid after a whisper or look.
  READ_TIMEOUT = 10
  # Seconds to wait for the solved message once every row is used.
  SOLVE_GRACE = 3
  # Most candidates listed in a status message.
  LIST_LIMIT = 40
  # Whispers in a row that may add no row before the script gives up.
  STALL_LIMIT = 2

  REDEEM_CONFIRM_PATTERN = /Once you redeem this, you'll have 1 instance access/
  REDEEMED_PATTERN = /You have just redeemed 1 instance of access/
  NO_REPRESENTATIVE_PATTERN = /isn't here!/
  ESCORTED_PATTERN = /The apprentice Timekeeper shows you to a time lock/
  TOUCH_CONFIRM_PATTERN = /This will consume a pass for Aesthene's Close/
  ATTUNED_PATTERN = /alarming pulse of energy surges from it and through you/
  ALREADY_ATTUNED_PATTERN = /already connected to the lock/

  # Parses arguments, loads the word lists and runs the chosen mode.
  #
  # @return [void]
  def initialize
    args = parse_args(arg_definitions)
    data = get_data('aesthene')
    @builtin_answers, = AestheneWords.normalize(data&.lock_answers)
    @solver = build_solver(data, get_settings)

    if args.check
      check_lock
    elsif args.solve
      attune_and_solve
    else
      redeem_slip
      attune_and_solve
    end
  end

  # @return [Array<Array<Hash>>] argument definitions for parse_args
  def arg_definitions
    [
      [{ name: 'full', regex: /^full$/i, description: 'Redeem a time slip, attune to the lock you are shown and solve it.' }],
      [{ name: 'solve', regex: /^solve$/i, description: 'Attune to (or resume) the lock in this room and solve it.' }],
      [{ name: 'check', regex: /^check$/i, description: 'List the answers still possible for the lock in this room.' }]
    ]
  end

  # Builds the solver from the shipped data and the character's additions.
  #
  # @param data [OpenStruct, nil] contents of data/base-aesthene.yaml
  # @param settings [OpenStruct] character settings
  # @return [AestheneSolver]
  def build_solver(data, settings)
    answers, rejected = AestheneWords.answers(data&.lock_answers, settings&.aesthene_lock_answers)
    unless rejected.empty?
      DRC.message("aesthene: ignoring aesthene_lock_answers entries that are not five letters: #{rejected.join(', ')}")
    end
    dictionary = AestheneWords.dictionary(data&.dictionary, answers)
    opening, = AestheneWords.normalize(data&.opening)
    abort_with('aesthene: no word lists found. Is data/base-aesthene.yaml installed?') if answers.empty? && dictionary.empty?

    AestheneSolver.new(answers, dictionary, opening: opening.first)
  end

  # Walks to the Timekeeper, redeems one time slip and asks to be shown to a
  # lock. Stops the script if any step fails.
  #
  # @return [void]
  def redeem_slip
    abort_with("aesthene: couldn't reach the apprentice Timekeeper (room #{TIMEKEEPER_ROOM}).") unless DRCT.walk_to(TIMEKEEPER_ROOM)
    abort_with('aesthene: no time slip found.') unless DRCI.in_hands?('time slip') || DRCI.get_item?('time slip')

    # The first REDEEM asks for confirmation; the second spends the slip.
    response = DRC.bput('redeem my slip', REDEEM_CONFIRM_PATTERN, REDEEMED_PATTERN, NO_REPRESENTATIVE_PATTERN)
    response = DRC.bput('redeem my slip', REDEEMED_PATTERN, NO_REPRESENTATIVE_PATTERN) if response.match?(REDEEM_CONFIRM_PATTERN)
    unless response.match?(REDEEMED_PATTERN)
      DRCI.stow_item?('time slip')
      abort_with('aesthene: the Timekeeper did not take the slip.')
    end

    return if DRC.bput('ask timekeeper about access', ESCORTED_PATTERN).match?(ESCORTED_PATTERN)

    abort_with('aesthene: the Timekeeper did not take you to a lock.')
  end

  # Attunes to the lock in this room, then guesses until it is solved.
  #
  # @return [void]
  def attune_and_solve
    reading = attune_to_lock
    solve(reading)
  end

  # Touches the lock to attune to it. Touching costs a pass, so the game asks
  # for a second touch to confirm.
  #
  # @return [AestheneGrid::Reading] the lock's state: empty for a fresh lock,
  #   the current grid when resuming one
  def attune_to_lock
    outcomes = [TOUCH_CONFIRM_PATTERN, ATTUNED_PATTERN, ALREADY_ATTUNED_PATTERN, AestheneGrid::NO_PASS_PATTERN]
    response = DRC.bput('touch lock', *outcomes)
    response = DRC.bput('touch lock', *outcomes.drop(1)) if response.match?(TOUCH_CONFIRM_PATTERN)

    case response
    when ATTUNED_PATTERN then AestheneGrid::Reading.new
    when ALREADY_ATTUNED_PATTERN then look_at_lock
    when AestheneGrid::NO_PASS_PATTERN then abort_with('aesthene: you need a redeemed pass. Try ;aesthene full.')
    else abort_with("aesthene: couldn't attune to a time lock here.")
    end
  end

  # Guesses until the lock is solved, it runs out of rows, nothing fits, or
  # the lock stops taking guesses.
  #
  # A whisper that adds no row is sent again once, since a reply such as
  # "...wait" drops it. The same state always picks the same guess, so
  # without a limit a lock that never takes it would be whispered forever.
  #
  # @param reading [AestheneGrid::Reading] the lock's current state
  # @return [void]
  def solve(reading)
    stalled = 0
    loop do
      @solver.observe(reading.rows)
      return report_solved(reading.rows.last&.guess || reading.whispered) if reading.solved?
      return report_failure('the lock has no rows left.') if reading.rows_left.zero?
      return report_failure("#{STALL_LIMIT} whispers in a row added no row to the lock.") if stalled >= STALL_LIMIT

      guess = @solver.next_guess(reading.rows_left)
      return report_failure('no word in the lists fits the feedback.') unless guess

      rows_left = reading.rows_left
      reading = whisper(guess)
      stalled = reading.rows_left < rows_left ? 0 : stalled + 1
    end
  end

  # Reads the lock and lists the answers still possible.
  #
  # @return [void]
  def check_lock
    reading = look_at_lock
    @solver.observe(reading.rows)
    report_candidates
    return if reading.solved? || reading.rows_left.zero?

    guess = @solver.next_guess(reading.rows_left)
    DRC.message("aesthene: suggested guess: #{guess}") if guess
  end

  # Whispers a guess and reads back the grid.
  #
  # @param guess [String]
  # @return [AestheneGrid::Reading]
  def whisper(guess)
    respond("aesthene: whispering #{guess} (#{@solver.candidates.size} possible)")
    reading = read_lock("whisper lock #{guess.downcase}")
    abort_with('aesthene: you are no longer attuned to the lock.') if %i[not_tasked no_pass].include?(reading.status)
    reading = look_at_lock unless reading.grid_complete? && reading.consistent?
    if reading.rows.last&.guess != guess
      DRC.message("aesthene: expected the last row to be #{guess} but read #{reading.rows.last&.guess || 'nothing'}.")
    end
    reading
  end

  # Looks at the lock and reads its grid.
  #
  # @return [AestheneGrid::Reading]
  def look_at_lock
    reading = read_lock('look lock')
    abort_with("aesthene: couldn't read the time lock.") unless reading.grid_complete?
    reading
  end

  # Sends a command and collects the game's lock output until it is settled
  # or the read times out.
  #
  # @param command [String]
  # @return [AestheneGrid::Reading]
  def read_lock(command)
    reading = AestheneGrid::Reading.new
    waitrt?
    clear
    put(command)
    deadline = Time.now + READ_TIMEOUT
    while Time.now < deadline
      line = get?
      if line.nil?
        pause 0.1
        next
      end
      reading.feed(line)
      break if reading.status
      next unless reading.grid_complete?
      break if command.start_with?('look')

      # Out of rows: the solved message, if any, follows the legend.
      deadline = [deadline, Time.now + SOLVE_GRACE].min if reading.out_of_rows?
    end
    reading
  end

  # Announces the answer, and asks for it to be reported when the built-in
  # list does not have it (it came from the dictionary or from the
  # character's aesthene_lock_answers).
  #
  # @param word [String]
  # @return [void]
  def report_solved(word)
    DRC.message("aesthene: solved! The word was #{word}.")
    return if @builtin_answers.include?(word)

    DRC.message("aesthene: #{word} is not in the built-in answer list. Please post it #{report_request}")
    DRC.message("aesthene: until then, add #{word} to aesthene_lock_answers in your YAML.") if @solver.fallback?
  end

  # @param reason [String]
  # @return [void]
  def report_failure(reason)
    DRC.message("aesthene: couldn't solve the lock: #{reason}")
    report_candidates
  end

  # Lists the candidates. With none left, the answer is in no word list, so
  # it asks for the answer to be reported once found.
  #
  # @return [void]
  def report_candidates
    candidates = @solver.candidates
    if candidates.empty?
      DRC.message("aesthene: the answer is not in any word list. Finish the lock by hand, then please post the answer #{report_request}")
      return
    end

    source = @solver.fallback? ? 'dictionary word' : 'known answer'
    source += 's' unless candidates.size == 1
    listed = candidates.first(LIST_LIMIT).join(', ')
    listed += ", ... (#{candidates.size - LIST_LIMIT} more)" if candidates.size > LIST_LIMIT
    DRC.message("aesthene: #{candidates.size} possible #{source}: #{listed}")
  end

  # Ends the messages asking for a missing answer to be reported, worded like
  # the other scripts' Discord requests.
  #
  # @return [String]
  def report_request
    "in the lich discord (listed in #{$clean_lich_char}links) so it can be added to the built-in list for everyone."
  end

  # Messages the reason and stops the script.
  #
  # @param reason [String]
  # @return [void]
  def abort_with(reason)
    DRC.message(reason)
    exit
  end
end

Aesthene.new
